PENDING — sweep: "could this return a valid-looking EMPTY result when the thing it
reads is BROKEN?"
Written 2026-09-12 after loadWatchState() silently discarded all verdict history on a
malformed file. NOT APPLIED (sandbox down all session). Read-only grep sweep of src/.

THE SHAPE
    try { return JSON.parse(readFileSync(F, 'utf8')); } catch { return <empty>; }
  "File is corrupt" and "nothing has happened yet" become the same value. Every
  downstream reader sees a clean, plausible zero. Second time this family has caused
  a real loss (loadUnlockEvents reading a non-existent path was the first).

================================================================================
RANKED BY CONSEQUENCE

1. src/core/routes.js:62  events = []        <- feeds assertTierRoutes()
   src/core/routes.js:77  unlockTokens = []  <- feeds checkClassifiersWired()
   *** WORST: THESE ARE BOOT GATES THAT PASS BECAUSE THEY READ NOTHING. ***
   A corrupt macro-calendar or unlocks.json makes "every tier has a reader" and
   "every classifier is wired" trivially TRUE — there is nothing left to route or
   classify. The gate reports OK and the bot starts with the thing the gate exists to
   protect entirely absent. A green check that cannot go red, arrived at from the
   input side.
   FIX: distinguish "read nothing" from "read an empty list". If the file exists and
   fails to parse, the assertion must FAIL, not pass. Boot should refuse.

2. src/core/taxonomy.js:135  equityTickers = new Set()
   A corrupt data/equity-tickers.json silently disables the EQUITY/xStock exclusion.
   Tokenised equities would stop being classified EXCLUDE and could be admitted to
   the universe. Silent, and safety-relevant rather than merely lossy.
   FIX: log [OPERATOR] and keep the previous in-memory set rather than emptying it;
   an empty exclusion list should never be reachable by accident.

3. src/sources/calendar/cadence-watch.js:28  loadWatchState -> { months:{}, demotions:{} }
   CONFIRMED HARM, 2026-09-12 (see PENDING-cliff-cache-staleness.pending). Total
   verdict history loss, silently, plus re-notification of an already-sent demote.
   FIX: quarantine to cadence-watch.corrupt-<ts>.json, log [OPERATOR], set
   historyResetAt, suppress demote DMs for the first cycle after a reset.

4. src/sources/calendar/cadence-watch.js:394  loadRecheckState -> { lastRun:null, rows:{} }
   A corrupt source-recheck.json reads as "the weekly recheck has never run". The
   overlay that marks sourced rows demoted/revised by their source disappears, so
   rows the SOURCE retracted quietly start pushing again. Same shape, opposite
   direction: silence restores alerts rather than suppressing them.

5. src/core/unclassified.js:41  cache = {}
   Corrupt file reads as "no unclassified announcement shapes ever seen". The
   heartbeat's backlog (105 shapes / 11 recurring today) resets to zero and the
   review queue vanishes with no trace.

6. src/sources/calendar/cadence-watch.js:165, 412, 475  catch { return; }
   A corrupt unlocks.json stops pollCadence / pollSourceRecheck / pollCliffWatch
   entirely, with NO log line. unlocks.js:35 logs this same failure properly
   ('[unlocks] bad unlocks.json') — these three do not. Inconsistent treatment of the
   identical failure in the same file.

7. src/sources/calendar/cadence-watch.js:520  tokens = []   (cadenceStatus)
   src/sources/calendar/unlocks.js:97        tokens = []   (sourcedFiring)
   The heartbeat then reports "nothing watched" / "0 sourced rows" as though that
   were the true state. The lines added to make silence visible would themselves go
   silent.

8. src/core/telemetry.js:208  catch { /* never run */ }  (restore drill)
   Conflates "drill never run" with "drill record corrupt". Low harm — both nag — but
   the nag names the wrong cause.

================================================================================
DOING IT RIGHT ALREADY — the patterns to copy
  src/sources/calendar/unlocks.js:35  logs '[unlocks] bad unlocks.json' and returns
                                      null, so the caller can tell broken from empty.
  src/sources/calendar/macro.js:55    logs '[macro] calendar unreadable'.
  src/core/outcomes.js:196, 203       PARSE-VERIFY BEFORE WRITE — a torn live file can
                                      never overwrite a good backup. The inverse
                                      discipline, already learned once.
  src/core/outcomes.js:45             no catch at all: a corrupt outcomes.json THROWS
  src/core/store.js:11                and takes the boot down loudly. Correct for
  src/index.js:33                     anything load-bearing.

THE RULE TO ADOPT
  A reader may return a default ONLY when it has established the file is ABSENT.
  If the file EXISTS and does not parse, that is an error: log [OPERATOR], and either
  throw (load-bearing state) or quarantine and mark the loss (accumulated history).
  Never the same value as "not started yet".

================================================================================
MAKE THE LOSS PERSIST — historyResetAt
  A log line scrolls and a DM is read once; a history loss matters for weeks. Same
  treatment as the stale-source ladder and the unreviewed-exclusion count:
    - on quarantine, write `historyResetAt` (+ the quarantined filename) into the
      fresh state;
    - the heartbeat carries "🚨 verdict history was RESET on <date> (file quarantined
      to X) — N verdicts lost, unacknowledged" on EVERY heartbeat until cleared;
    - clearing is an explicit operator action (the annotate/acknowledge write path),
      never automatic and never a timeout.

================================================================================
TURN THE ACCIDENT INTO A FIXTURE — determinism of the watch
  The 2026-09-12 reset accidentally re-derived EIGEN 2026-08 CONFIRM 0.976,
  MOVE 2026-09 CONFIRM 2.048 / 19,376,705 and ENA 2026-09 DEMOTE 5,148,798 EXACTLY.
  That is evidence for a property the whole re-score design depends on and which has
  never been tested deliberately: SCORING IS DETERMINISTIC OVER FIXED INPUTS. Nothing
  can be safely re-scored if re-scoring can disagree with itself.
  FIXTURE: freeze one byDay fixture per row shape (single, family, contract-cliff),
  run cadenceDecision / cliffClusterDecision TWICE over it with a fixed `now`, and
  assert deep equality of the verdict objects — action, ratio, amounts, window, the
  lot. Then mutate one input and assert the verdict CHANGES, so the test can go red.
  Pin the three live values above as the regression case, since they are known-good
  and were reproduced independently.
